00:02:29.431 --> 00:02:30.820
That's not the way you do it,

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.070
you have to do it on the chest area.

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:33.923
- I can't stand it!

00:02:33.923 --> 00:02:36.660
- I'll give you something
for the pain, just hold on.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:39.030
Notify the orthopaedic
we have an open fracture.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:41.800
Give him tetanus and
diamorphine right away!

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.730
- The reason why they say
specifically open fracture,

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.720
that means that your bone has broken

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.190
and has penetrated out of your skin.

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:51.130
So that's dangerous for two reasons.

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:53.230
Number one, high chance of infection

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:54.740
because you have an open wound.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.139
Second, because sometimes
the bone can put pressure

00:02:58.139 --> 00:03:00.464
on your blood vessels, and therefore

00:03:00.464 --> 00:03:03.880
cause something known as claudication.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:04.900
Which means that you're not getting

00:03:04.900 --> 00:03:06.602
enough circulation to a part of the body,

00:03:06.602 --> 00:03:09.400
and then that area can swell and it can be

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:11.530
very dangerous and you need
emergen surgery for that.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:13.940
And then on top of it,
you could obviously lose

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:16.470
a lot, a lot of blood, because you have

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:19.513
an open fracture that you need
to get closed and reduced.

00:03:21.397 --> 00:03:22.330
- Come on back to us.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:23.163
Come on, baby.

00:03:23.163 --> 00:03:25.500
- I don't know where his
hands are in that scene.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.270
Just because you're seeing
the electrical activity

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.040
